# `class_pattern_certainty` reduces the pattern through class ordering, and the
# ordering is `:unknown` for a class no RBS declares — which is `:maybe`, the one
# answer this fixture must not get for free. So the shadowing class is declared
# here, exactly as https://github.com/rigortype/rigor/issues/655 reports it (the
# issue's `sig/app.rbs`), and the core `Random` it shadows is already known.

module Bar
  module Nested
    class Random
      def nested_only: () -> String
    end
  end
end
